ns\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7 dev 5, master [1c8cc9e]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev5 - Fedora Linux 43.20260423.0 (Kinoite) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (nvidia; 580.142) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900XT 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 62.71 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nAfter following the steps for HDR output, I've been busy working with a beautiful HDR workflow in 3D. However, every time I open a new editor window, the editor would be in SDR. I would have to uncheck and recheck Request HDR Output in Project Settings to enable HDR output again. \n\nI'm using Fedora Kinoite 43 with a KDE Plasma Wayland session. The same happens in Gnome 49.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Follow the steps provided in the [documentation page](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/rendering/hdr_output.html).\n2. Click on Project > Reload Current Project.\n3. Open Project > Project Settings...\n4. To re-enable HDR, uncheck `display/window/hdr/request_hdr_output` and check it again\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Godot HDR Output demo](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/misc/hdr_output), with `res://tonemap/tonemap.tscn` loaded as main scene.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.co